71,[[0,346]],[["a5223355_362e4af6",64,0,1,"Why is this expect_true before lifecycle events? I would expect a size but no time, yet?"]],0,510],[7140893,20405,175,2.983,2.275,[[0,0.661,347,116],[2,0.317,127,57],[6,0.011,57,1],[14,0.011,48,1]],[["38b9f8aa_33cb5529",9,-1,1,"Do you know if this is actually still true?"],["4c9ce03f_7fcf8b64",9,-1,1,"Is the \"but it could\" theoretical or do you know of a case? (I understand the emitted to timeline part). Perhaps it could increase reporting during abandonment? (A good thing!)"],["95612e36_b6c70330",3,-1,1,"FWIW we discussed this issue at TPAC this week and committed to changing it in spec and implementation (for FF and Chrome to align with WebKit).…"],["c12df71b_2fecf2af",9,-1,1,"Given the comment above, I'd also support just fixing this immediately for interop. This will not change final LCP scores, but it could improve RUM insights or even ability to measure LCP (i.e. for…"]],0,511],[7157755,20406,292,4.91,3.884,[[2,128]],[],0,512],[7158664,20406,57,0.974,0.71,[[2,0.617,129,36],[0,0.383,348,21]],[],0,513],[7164599,20410,7,0.224,0.147,[[0,349]],[],0,514],[7137609,20411,29,0.519,0.379,[[0,350]],[],0,515],[7164696,20411,119,1.636,1.222,[[0,351]],[["c7773b31_6584bb9e",3,0,0,"Huh, I had thought that the FCP path was entirely separate from LCP path-- I guess that for something like body-opacity-0, we might not technically re-paint content and so not observe FCP, but we…"],["f583bbef_b1a9895e",9,0,1,"Nit: incorrect -> imperfect i.e. this is correct for LCP, just not sufficient for other paint metrics."]],0,516],[7180683,20413,36,0.974,0.71,[[0,352]],[],0,517],[7162896,20424,429,4.91,3.884,[[0,0.758,353,333],[2,0.093,130,35],[1,0.071,19,30],[17,0.036,31,15],[6,0.024,58,10],[5,0.009,15,3],[18,0.009,6,3]],[],0,518],[7219412,20428,144,2.983,2.275,[[0,354]],[["9a284c2f_4d87192d",65,-3,0,"Is this comment correct? I see that size is updated immediately, but looks like time is still null? Is it different for UKM?"]],0,519],[7118112,20433,97,1.636,1.222,[[0,355]],[["8216e58b_c64674ab",64,-1,1,"Nit: should you have an expect_true for this first, above? (you added it to the other opacity test above)"]],0,520],[7248299,20433,106,1.636,1.222,[[2,0.798,131,86],[0,0.202,356,20]],[["fb6455d9_6cb6005b",66,-1,1,"textContent?"]],0,521],[7257199,20437,53,0.974,0.71,[[0,357]],[],0,522],[7256268,20437,74,1.636,1.222,[[0,358]],[["7724a452_4badbb13",0,0,1,"My understanding was that this automatically happens after dispose for HeapHashSet of pure weakness members?…"],["c13638c2_0ff9e54a",14,0,0,"Would we report less histograms (for the failed-to-emit cases) with these guards, and the timing of Dispose now vs prior? I think it's fine to break these but should consider what type of reporting…"],["4b3c1f8b_e8f4eab8",0,3,0,"Hi folks. I believe this CL is introducing a bug. Specifically, this `Contains` check will always return false. `potential_soft_navigations_` is a `HeapHashSet<WeakMember<SoftNavigationContext>>`.…"]],0,523],[7120640,20438,251,2.983,2.275,[[0,0.961,359,242],[2,0.039,132,9]],[["0b489549_0ffd2b9b",0,-5,0,"I think today this could be a CHECK today? But might change if we start to emit ICP always, as the TODO in `UpdateSoftLcpCandidate` suggests? In which case, the name of `context_for_current_url_`…"],["17936075_dbb383b9",14,-5,0,"I guess this affects more than just Paint->Presentation, it also could be: - Interaction - Network, Routing, Dom update, Paint... - ... - URL (finally) It's more common to set URL before or during…"],["39a27306_969badb7",14,-5,0,"Since we are moving PerfEntry creation into this class for the ICP entry, I wonder if we should do the same for Soft-Nav (and hard-LCP?) Looking at WindowPerformance, most apis do just pass data and…"],["61174c97_fa172f4e",3,-5,0,"Nit: technically this is requested of us, and we might in theory. But, I still think the LCP calculator could consider the pair of largest image and text as a single candidate that it emits together,…"],["74777426_b324fa20",14,-5,0,"Hmmm, we guard the actual emit further down, anyway: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/timing/window_performance.cc;l=1564-1567 And along the…"],["7583a2a8_42dac9d3",14,-5,0,"In hindsight I wonder if this should have had \"LCP\" in its name-- since there are 2 types of perf entry this class manages, its ambiguous without knowing which base class we override..."],["8935213d_8ae9221f",12,-5,1,"Could we Emit a soft-nav without an ICP? (I guess yes, until we \"harden\"?)"],["96f05eb5_f0e25da0",14,-5,1,"Nit: maybe just remove this part of the comment now?"],["ab70a643_fe3993df",67,-5,0,"I'm fine with this, but FYI `AddLongAnimationFrameEntry` just uses the base class PerformanceEntry* to avoid the type declaration."],["d2e3379e_0b445385",14,-5,0,"Similarly, we could leave this unenforced. Obviously we don't need to create entries if we aren't going to expose them, which is what the flag guards-- but now we are sort of using the entry as a…"],["e903754f_5191219d",3,-5,0,"I like that. Also, I think post-OT we want to change to not hold back ICP entries, anyway."],["f0c5611b_e9225b7e",0,-5,1,"Nit: I think this this is specifically about soft-LCP and might be worth keeping in the name?"],["bdd5a3de_5cbcd0d5",12,0,1,"I guess the main reason for doing it at paint time is to increment navigationID so that other entries are segmented accordingly. Otherwise the timing of the navigationID change is based on arbitrary…"],["cce09612_c9cb6001",14,0,0,"Maybe move this below the flag check now? Or do you want to do that in a separate patch? Connor mentioned NOT guarding trace events on flag settings, but I think we decided to start with consistency…"]],0,524],[7278708,20441,254,2.983,2.275,[[0,0.961,360,241],[2,0.039,133,9]],[],0,525]]}